    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d944">

                <pb facs="1092" n="898" xml:id="pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Pauley Files</note>
                <head>No. 944<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Representative on the Allied Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-28">July 28, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for Ambassador
                        Pauley</hi></p>
                <p>The attached memorandum for U. S. Group CC<anchor n="1" xml:id="d944-f1"/> raises
                    certain questions regarding restitution of art objects.</p>
                <p>I believe that we might concur in recommendations 1 and 2, and I should like your
                    comments on recommendation 3. It too would seem acceptable, subject to your
                    views on “replacement” as against straight restitution of art objects.</p>
                <p>It would be desirable if we could get off a joint memorandum on this subject to
                    General Clay.</p>
                <closer><signed>W L C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">layton</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d944-f1" n="1" xml:id="d944-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. For the recommendations referred to in the following paragraph, see
                    the subenclosure to <ref target="#d964">document No. 964</ref>.</p>
            </note>
